{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836800",
      "title": "How NOT To Send HTTP Requests (And Why It's Wrong)",
      "sourceHash": "326f716bbb6f203211414329f2f67fc6f8133884dee954bf00fc62b5b07225e4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 3.36,
          "en": "Now an HTTP request can be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.36,
          "end": 6.9,
          "en": "in a client site project in different ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.9,
          "end": 10.503,
          "en": "For example, with help of the built-in fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 14.88,
          "en": "This is a function that's not provided by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.88,
          "end": 18.09,
          "en": "but instead directly by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.09,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "And fetch is a function that can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 25.533,
          "en": "to send an HTTP request to some other server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "Now, unlike the name might imply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "you can actually not just use it to fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 35.793,
          "en": "but also to send data, but we'll explore that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 41.99,
          "en": "In its simplest form, fetch wants the URL of the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 45.333,
          "en": "you wanna send a request to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 50.07,
          "en": "Now herein this project I provided to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 55.07,
          "en": "that's http://localhost 3000",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.37,
          "end": 58.113,
          "en": "separated by a colon here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.12,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "This URL will target my running backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 69.44,
          "en": "And then there it's this /places path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 73.56,
          "en": "that we wanna target to get back the places data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.56,
          "end": 76.383,
          "en": "that's stored in a file on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 81.60300000000001,
          "en": "So therefore here we should append /places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 82.92,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "Now out of the box, this will send a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 90.513,
          "en": "to this URL, which is indeed exactly what we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 91.77,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "Now fetch then returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 99.63,
          "en": "which is a JavaScript value that will eventually resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "to another value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 103.89,
          "en": "So it's basically a wrapper object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 103.89,
          "end": 106.95,
          "en": "around a value that's not there yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "but that will eventually be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 111.63,
          "en": "In this case, it's a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 111.63,
          "end": 115.413,
          "en": "around an eventually received response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 116.25,
          "end": 119.13,
          "en": "So a promise is a standard JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "that will yield different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 124.59,
          "en": "depending on the state of that promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.59,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "And to access those different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 131.433,
          "en": "you can chain methods on the result of calling fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 132.3,
          "end": 134.85,
          "en": "You can add the then method, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 134.85,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "and pass a function to the then method to define a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "that should be executed once this promise resolved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 144.87,
          "en": "and the response is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 147.99,
          "en": "And here in this function, you would then automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 150.453,
          "en": "receive that response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 151.53,
          "end": 154.56,
          "en": "But this function, which you're passing to then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 157.14,
          "en": "will be executed by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 157.14,
          "end": 159.12,
          "en": "only once the response is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 159.12,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "So not instantly, but at some point in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 167.94,
          "en": "Now in modern JavaScript, you can also use the await keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 167.94,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "to access this response like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "and to have a more readable syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 176.4,
          "en": "But this is only available if the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.4,
          "end": 179.97,
          "en": "in which this code executes is decorated with async,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.97,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "which on the other hand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "is not allowed for component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 187.53,
          "en": "That's a restriction implied by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.53,
          "end": 189.93,
          "en": "So we can't use async await here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.93,
          "end": 192.483,
          "en": "but we will soon use it in some other place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 196.17000000000002,
          "en": "So here I'll go back to that other notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.17000000000002,
          "end": 199.53,
          "en": "which does work where we got the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.53,
          "end": 202.71,
          "en": "and where we can define which code should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.71,
          "end": 204.483,
          "en": "once the response is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "Now, when using this fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "this response object will have some other methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 214.71,
          "en": "that can be used to access the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 217.11,
          "en": "that's part of the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 219.9,
          "en": "For example, the JS method can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.9,
          "end": 223.92000000000002,
          "en": "to extract data that's attached in the JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.92000000000002,
          "end": 227.88,
          "en": "And JSON is simply a text-based data format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 232.2,
          "en": "that looks like this here in the places.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 232.2,
          "end": 233.57999999999998,
          "en": "this is how it looks like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.57999999999998,
          "end": 237.3,
          "en": "basically like a JavaScript array and object you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.3,
          "end": 239.57999999999998,
          "en": "But all the keys are wrapped with quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.57999999999998,
          "end": 241.78,
          "en": "That's a special feature of JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.81,
          "end": 247.08,
          "en": "and JSON is the facto standard data format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 247.08,
          "end": 250.053,
          "en": "for exchanging data with backends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 255.12,
          "en": "Now this JSON method returns another promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.12,
          "end": 257.64,
          "en": "and therefore if I return JSON here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.64,
          "end": 261.84,
          "en": "we can add another then method after the first then method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 261.84,
          "end": 264.72,
          "en": "to eventually get back our response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 266.433,
          "en": "and work with that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 271.023,
          "en": "And that's how you can chain those different then calls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.89,
          "end": 275.52,
          "en": "And here we then got the final response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 275.52,
          "end": 280.52,
          "en": "which in case of this dummy API here should be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 287.21,
          "en": "that has a places key where we then have the places data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 291.78,
          "en": "so this array of available places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 291.78,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "And therefore here we can access resData.places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 300.33,
          "en": "in this case for this dummy API to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 300.33,
          "end": 302.673,
          "en": "to this array of available places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "And now we could call set available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 310.113,
          "en": "and pass that data to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 311.46,
          "end": 316.46,
          "en": "But this code here has a huge flaw and problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 317.49,
          "end": 320.2,
          "en": "It would create an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.48,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "because when calling fetch like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 326.37,
          "en": "directly in the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 326.37,
          "end": 329.04,
          "en": "this code of course will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 329.04,
          "end": 331.75,
          "en": "every time the component function executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 332.88,
          "end": 335.61,
          "en": "and therefore a new request would be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 335.61,
          "end": 338.043,
          "en": "whenever this component function executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 338.97,
          "end": 342.39,
          "en": "The problem is that in the second then block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 342.39,
          "end": 344.31,
          "en": "we then update the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 344.31,
          "end": 347.37,
          "en": "which of course causes this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 347.37,
          "end": 349.02,
          "en": "to execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 349.02,
          "end": 352.77,
          "en": "So we would end up with a new request, a new state update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 352.77,
          "end": 356.7,
          "en": "a new execution, a new request, a new state update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 356.7,
          "end": 358.293,
          "en": "and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 359.79,
          "end": 363.27,
          "en": "And therefore we can't send the request like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 363.27,
          "end": 368.27,
          "en": "But thankfully, if you went through the side effects section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 368.64,
          "end": 372.15,
          "en": "this problem might sound familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 372.15,
          "end": 374.28,
          "en": "And if you went through that section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 374.28,
          "end": 377.01,
          "en": "you are also aware of a solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 377.01,
          "end": 380.61,
          "en": "We can useEffect to wrap this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 380.61,
          "end": 382.773,
          "en": "and to avoid this infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}